<Legal title="Privacy Policy | SIRYUS" description="How Siryus Creative Media Ltd collects, uses and protects personal data across siryushub.com, SIRYUS A.M, SIGNAL. and ARC. Creatives." path="/privacy-policy">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-page__meta">Effective date: 2 November 2026</p>

  <div class="summary">
    <p><strong>In short:</strong> we collect only what you choose to send us through our forms, plus the basic technical data any website needs to run safely. We use it to reply to you, provide our services and keep our sites secure. We never sell your data. You can ask to see, correct or delete it at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:contact@siryushub.com">contact@siryushub.com</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <ol class="toc">
    <li><a href="#who">Who we are</a></li>
    <li><a href="#scope">What this policy covers</a></li>
    <li><a href="#collect">What we collect</a></li>
    <li><a href="#use">How and why we use it</a></li>
    <li><a href="#share">Who we share it with</a></li>
    <li><a href="#transfers">International transfers</a></li>
    <li><a href="#keep">How long we keep it</a></li>
    <li><a href="#rights">Your rights</a></li>
    <li><a href="#security">Security</a></li>
    <li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
    <li><a href="#marketing">Marketing emails</a></li>
    <li><a href="#changes">Changes and contact</a></li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>Siryus Creative Media Ltd ("SIRYUS", "we", "us") is a company registered in Nigeria with its head office in Abuja. We are the data controller for personal data collected through the websites listed in section 2. That means we decide why and how your data is used, and we are responsible for it.</p>
  <p>For any privacy question or request, contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@siryushub.com">contact@siryushub.com</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="scope">2. What this policy covers</h2>
  <p>This policy applies to the following websites, each run by Siryus Creative Media Ltd:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>siryushub.com</strong>, the SIRYUS home site</li>
    <li><strong>artists.siryushub.com</strong>, SIRYUS A.M</li>
    <li><strong>growth.siryushub.com</strong>, SIGNAL. by SIRYUS</li>
    <li><strong>collective.siryushub.com</strong>, ARC. Creatives</li>
  </ul>
  <p>It also covers emails we exchange with you because of those sites. It does not cover PAVO Create (pavocreate.com), which is a separate company with its own policies, or any other website we link to.</p>
  <p>If you sign a written agreement with us, for example for music distribution, management or marketing services, that agreement may contain further privacy terms. Where it does, those terms apply alongside this policy.</p>

  <h2 id="collect">3. What we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>What we collect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Contact and meeting request forms on SIRYUS A.M and SIGNAL.</td><td>Your name and email address, plus anything you choose to add: artist, company or brand name, the service you are interested in, a link to your music, a budget range, a preferred meeting time and your message.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>The ARC. Letter sign-up on ARC. Creatives</td><td>Your email address.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Emails you send us</td><td>Your email address, name and whatever you include in your message or attachments.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Please do not send us sensitive personal data (for example about health, religious beliefs or finances) through our forms unless it is needed for your request. If you do, we will use it only to deal with that request.</p>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <p>Our websites are hosted and protected by Cloudflare. When you visit, Cloudflare processes technical data such as your IP address, browser type, device type, the pages you request and the time of your visit. This is used to deliver the pages, protect the sites against attacks and bots, and produce aggregate, cookieless visitor statistics. Cloudflare may set strictly necessary security cookies. See our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for details.</p>
  <p>We do not use advertising trackers, social media pixels or tools that build a profile of you across other websites.</p>

  <h2 id="use">4. How and why we use it</h2>
  <p>We only use personal data when the law allows it. Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 and, for visitors in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, the GDPR and UK GDPR, we rely on these lawful bases:</p>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Lawful basis</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Replying to your enquiry and arranging a meeting</td><td>Our legitimate interest in responding to people who contact us, and taking steps at your request before entering into a contract</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Providing services you have agreed to buy</td><td>Performance of a contract with you</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sending the ARC. Letter</td><td>Your consent, which you can withdraw at any time</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Keeping our websites secure and working, and understanding overall traffic</td><td>Our legitimate interest in running safe, reliable websites</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Keeping records for tax, accounting and legal purposes, and handling legal claims</td><td>Compliance with legal obligations, and our legitimate interest in defending our rights</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>Where we rely on legitimate interests, we have balanced them against your rights and expectations. You can object at any time (see section 8). We do not make decisions about you based solely on automated processing.</p>

  <h2 id="share">5. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent or trade personal data. We share it only with service providers who help us run our sites and business, under contracts that require them to protect it and use it only on our instructions:</p>
  <div class="table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>What they do</th><th>Location</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare, Inc.</td><td>Website hosting, content delivery, security and email forwarding for our @siryushub.com addresses</td><td>Global network, headquartered in the United States</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mailjet (Sinch)</td><td>Sending the emails generated by our contact forms</td><td>European Union</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Formspree, Inc.</td><td>Receiving ARC. Letter sign-ups</td><td>United States</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Google LLC</td><td>Email inboxes our team uses to read and answer messages</td><td>United States</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>We may also disclose personal data if the law requires it, to protect our rights or the safety of others, or as part of a sale, merger or reorganisation of our business, in which case the recipient must protect it in line with this policy.</p>
  <p>Our websites link to other services such as Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube and Instagram. When you follow those links, the other service's privacy policy applies.</p>

  <h2 id="transfers">6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Some of our providers process data outside Nigeria, including in the United States and the European Union. When we transfer personal data abroad, we do so in line with Part VIII of the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 and, where relevant, the GDPR. We rely on safeguards such as the provider's standard contractual clauses, data processing agreements and certifications, and we choose providers with recognised security standards.</p>

  <h2 id="keep">7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enquiries that do not lead to work:</strong> up to 24 months after our last contact, then deleted.</li>
    <li><strong>Client and artist records:</strong> for the length of our relationship and then for as long as the law requires for tax, accounting and limitation purposes, generally up to 6 years after it ends.</li>
    <li><strong>ARC. Letter subscribers:</strong> until you unsubscribe. We then keep only a note of your address so we do not email you again.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical and security logs:</strong> for the short periods set by Cloudflare, usually days or weeks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="rights">8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023, and the GDPR or UK GDPR where they apply, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>be told how your data is used, which is what this policy does;</li>
    <li>get a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
    <li>have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected;</li>
    <li>have your data deleted when we no longer need it or have no lawful basis to keep it;</li>
    <li>ask us to limit how we use your data;</li>
    <li>object to our use of your data based on legitimate interests, and to direct marketing at any time;</li>
    <li>receive data you gave us in a commonly used, machine-readable format, and have it sent to another organisation where technically possible;</li>
    <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting anything we did before you withdrew it; and</li>
    <li>not be subject to decisions based solely on automated processing that significantly affect you.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To use any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:contact@siryushub.com">contact@siryushub.com</a>. We may need to confirm your identity. We will respond within 30 days, and tell you if we need longer for a complex request. Using your rights is free unless a request is clearly unfounded or excessive.</p>
  <p>If you are unhappy with how we handle your data, please talk to us first. You also have the right to complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission (<a href="https://ndpc.gov.ng" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ndpc.gov.ng</a>) or, if you live in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, to your local data protection authority.</p>

  <h2 id="security">9. Security</h2>
  <p>We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data. These include encrypted connections (HTTPS) on all our sites, access limited to people who need it, reputable providers with strong security practices, and spam and abuse protection on our forms. No system is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security. If a personal data breach is likely to put your rights at risk, we will notify the Nigeria Data Protection Commission within 72 hours of becoming aware of it and tell you without undue delay where the law requires.</p>

  <h2 id="children">10. Children</h2>
  <p>Our websites are not aimed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 18 without the consent of a parent or guardian. Artists under 18 who want to work with SIRYUS A.M should contact us with a parent or guardian. If you believe a child has sent us personal data without consent, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

  <h2 id="marketing">11. Marketing emails</h2>
  <p>We only send newsletters, such as the ARC. Letter, to people who sign up. Every newsletter includes a way to unsubscribe, and you can also email us to stop them. Replying to an enquiry or sending service updates to clients is not marketing.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">12. Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy when our sites, services or the law change. We will post the new version here with a new effective date and, if the changes are significant, tell people we have an active relationship with.</p>
  <p>Siryus Creative Media Ltd, Abuja, Nigeria. Email: <a href="mailto:contact@siryushub.com">contact@siryushub.com</a></p>
</Legal>
